# Files, saving and versions

Radii Office apps save ordinary files that you own. This page explains the file types, where your work is kept, and how to get it out.


::divider{aqua}
## File types

| Extension | Made by | What it is |
| --- | --- | --- |
| #G#.kd#= | Writeout, OpenDB | A Keydown document: a short header and then readable text |
| #TU#.kn#= | Bitbook | A Keydown note |
| #T#.ka#= | Amber | A presentation |
| #C#.kv#= | Inkpath | A vector drawing |
| #B#.kb#= | Mainkey | A record database |
| #PR#.kfe#= #PR#.kfv#= #PR#.kfa#= | Formly | An editable form, a viewable form, and the answers |
| #PK#.ics#= #PK#.kh#= | Hexa | Calendar events (standard iCalendar) and Hexa's own format |
| #R#.tk#= | Taskra | A to-do list |
| #O#.kc#= | Cabinet | A drawer shared as a file |

Because the Keydown files are plain text, you can open them in any text editor, and Writeout and Bitbook can open each other's files!

## Where your work lives

* #C.marker(In the browser.) Apps keep your documents on this computer, in the browser's own storage, so they are there when you come back. Nothing is uploaded!
* #B.marker(In a file on your computer.) Use **Share > Keep a file on this computer** (Chrome, Edge and Opera) to link a document to a real file. The app then saves to it automatically!
* #PR.marker(On a shared link.) Sharing is separate and always your choice. See [Sharing and live editing](#/sharing)!

::warning Clearing site data deletes browser copies
If you clear your browser's site data, documents kept only in the browser are removed. Export or keep a file on your computer for anything important!
::end

## The documents library

Writeout, Bitbook and other apps share a documents library. Each document has its own address ending in `?file=` and an id, so the address always reopens that document. Opening an app without an address reopens the document you used last!

## Version history

Choose **File > Version history** (or **Review > Version History** in Writeout) to see earlier copies of a document. Apps take a snapshot as you work, and #TU.torpedo(Save Version) takes one on purpose. Pick one to preview it and restore it!

## Getting your work out

* #G.prism(Save a Copy) and #PK.torpedo(Export) (on the File screen) write a file to your computer!
* Writeout exports PDF, Word (`.docx`), OpenDocument (`.odt`), plain text and EPUB, and both Writeout and Bitbook can #PK.torpedo(Print)!
* Inkpath exports SVG and PNG, and Imbuer and Mainkey import and export CSV!
* Hexa exports `.ics`, and Zonerider exports glTF, OBJ and STL!
* Every app's data is yours: there is no lock-in, and the source is public!
